From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 14:50:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Replaced sizing: CSS naturals for SVG images, no-stretch
 integration
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Companion to taffy's no-stretch-for-replaced change. Four pieces:

- parse_svg_image normalizes the usvg viewport to the CSS natural
  dimensions: usvg resolves a missing axis against the viewBox edge
  (width=100 + viewBox 200x200 gave a 100x200 tree) and the painted
  tree is scaled to the layout box, so any tree/naturals mismatch
  letterboxed the content. Derived axes (ratio or 300/150 default)
  and the dimensionless 300x150 case are stamped onto the root.
- The measure path computes SVG inherent size from the naturals;
  ratio-only documents carry natural_ratio so block-level boxes fill
  the available inline size (CSS2 §10.3.2) while inline-level ones
  contain-fit 300x150, and dimensionless documents read the default
  object size with NO ratio coupling between axes.
- item_is_replaced is stamped onto the taffy style for img/canvas/
  iframe/svg so block layout skips stretch-fitting them.
- The aspect-ratio stamp derives from the naturals instead of the
  usvg-synthesized size (which lied for dimensionless documents).

Against blitz-dom 0.3.0-beta.3: the taffy style is no longer stored on
the node, upstream sets IS_REPLACED itself and the aspect-ratio stamp
(old patch "Lift replaced elements' intrinsic ratio") is gone, so the
damage.rs half of this change no longer applies.
